<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ohrigstad</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Andries-Ohrigstad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ohrigstad, originally Andries-Ohrigstad, is a small town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mpumalanga">Mpumalanga</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-africa">South Africa</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/voortrekkers">Voortrekkers</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andries-hendrik-potgieter">Andries Hendrik Potgieter</a> founded it in 1845 as the capital of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boers">Boer</a> settlement beyond British reach, naming it after Potgieter and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> merchant Georgius Ohrig. Malaria drove the settlers out, and in 1849 they founded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lydenburg">Lydenburg</a> as a new centre.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ohrigstad.jpg" alt="Ohrigstad" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michaelphillipr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ohrigstad.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
